pub static FALLBACKS_JSON: &str = r####"{"ielts_task1":{"topic":"Global Internet Usage Trends","prompt_text":"The bar chart below shows the percentage of internet users in six different countries in 2010 and 2020. Summarise the information by selecting and reporting the main features, and make comparisons where relevant. Write at least 150 words.","supplementary_data":{"chart_description":"Bar chart showing internet usage percentages: USA (74% in 2010, 90% in 2020), UK (85% in 2010, 95% in 2020), Japan (78% in 2010, 92% in 2020), Brazil (41% in 2010, 75% in 2020), India (7.5% in 2010, 45% in 2020), Nigeria (24% in 2010, 55% in 2020)."},"difficulty":"intermediate"},"ielts_task2":{"topic":"Technology in Education","prompt_text":"Some people believe that technology has made education more accessible and effective, while others argue that it has created new problems such as distraction and inequality. Discuss both views and give your own opinion. Write at least 250 words.","difficulty":"intermediate"},"toefl_integrated":{"topic":"Remote Work Benefits","prompt_text":"Summarize the points made in the lecture, being sure to explain how they challenge the specific points made in the reading passage.","supplementary_data":{"reading_passage":"Remote work has been widely praised for its numerous benefits to both employees and employers. Studies have shown that remote workers report higher job satisfaction, as they can create personalized work environments and eliminate stressful commutes. Companies benefit from reduced overhead costs, as they need less office space. Furthermore, remote work allows businesses to tap into a global talent pool, hiring the best candidates regardless of geographic location.","lecture_summary":"However, the professor argues that remote work has significant drawbacks that are often overlooked. First, remote workers frequently report feelings of isolation and disconnection from their teams. Second, the blurring of work-life boundaries often leads to longer working hours and burnout. Third, not all employees have access to adequate home office setups, creating inequality among workers."},"difficulty":"intermediate"},"toefl_independent":{"topic":"Living in Cities vs Rural Areas","prompt_text":"Do you agree or disagree with the following statement? Living in a large city is better than living in a small town or rural area. Use specific reasons and examples to support your answer.","difficulty":"intermediate"},"celpip":{"topic":"Workplace Schedule Change","prompt_text":"Your company has announced that it will be changing from a five-day work week to a four-day work week with longer hours each day. Write an email to your manager expressing your opinion about this change. Include your thoughts on how this will affect your work and any suggestions you have.","difficulty":"intermediate"},"cambridge_fce":{"topic":"Benefits of Learning Languages","prompt_text":"You have had a class discussion about the importance of learning foreign languages. Your teacher has asked you to write an essay. Write your essay using all the notes and giving reasons for your point of view. \"Learning a foreign language is essential for everyone.\" Notes: 1. Career opportunities 2. Cultural understanding 3. Your own idea. Write 140-190 words.","difficulty":"intermediate"},"cambridge_cae":{"topic":"Local Environmental Initiative","prompt_text":"An international environmental organization is looking for proposals from local communities for green initiatives. Write a proposal for your local area, explaining the current environmental challenges, your proposed solution, and the expected benefits. Write 220-260 words.","difficulty":"advanced"},"duolingo":{"topic":"Favorite Place to Visit","prompt_text":"Describe a place you love to visit and explain why it is special to you. Write 50-100 words.","difficulty":"beginner"},"pte":{"topic":"Impact of Social Media","prompt_text":"Social media has fundamentally changed how people communicate and access information. Some argue it has made society more connected, while others believe it has led to increased isolation and misinformation. Discuss both perspectives and provide your own view. Write 200-300 words.","difficulty":"intermediate"},"general_email":{"topic":"Request for Time Off","prompt_text":"Write a formal email to your manager requesting two weeks of vacation leave next month. Explain why you need the time off, suggest how your responsibilities can be covered, and ask for approval. Write 100-200 words.","difficulty":"intermediate"},"general_essay":{"topic":"Importance of Reading Books","prompt_text":"In the digital age, fewer people read books for pleasure. Do you think reading books is still important? Why or why not? Support your argument with specific reasons and examples. Write 200-400 words.","difficulty":"intermediate"},"general_letter":{"topic":"Thank You to a Mentor","prompt_text":"Write a letter to someone who has been a mentor or role model in your life. Thank them for their guidance, describe how they have influenced you, and share what you have achieved as a result. Write 150-250 words.","difficulty":"intermediate"},"general_report":{"topic":"Customer Satisfaction Survey Results","prompt_text":"You conducted a customer satisfaction survey at your workplace. Write a report summarizing the key findings, highlighting areas of concern, and recommending improvements. Write 200-350 words.","difficulty":"intermediate"}}"####;
